      <h2>What goes in each issue</h2>

      <h3>1. Tip</h3>
      <p>One specific, useful lesson from a recent build, in two to four plain sentences. It teaches something you can use on your own, whether or not you ever hire me.</p>

      <h3>2. Update</h3>
      <p>One thing I published recently, such as a new sample site or an updated service page, in a sentence or two with a link. It shows what I&apos;ve been working on and improving.</p>

      <h3>3. Ask</h3>
      <p>One gentle request, different each time. Sometimes it&apos;s "Know someone in [trade] who needs a better website? Forward this." It&apos;s always a light touch.</p>

      <h2>Why every other week</h2>
      <p>Weekly is more than I can write at the standard I want, and monthly is too rare to stay in mind. Every other week leaves room for something useful each time. If I have nothing useful to say in a given week, I skip that issue.</p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>The list runs on <a href="https://buttondown.com" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">an independent email service built for privacy</a>. I use your email address only to send you the newsletter, with no tracking pixels and no third-party ad targeting. Every issue has a one-click unsubscribe link. The full <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="inline-link">privacy policy</a> covers the rest.</p>

      <h2>Archive</h2>
      <p>Past issues will appear on this page once the third one is live.</p>
